  "immersionFoot": "Immersion foot",
  "@immersionFoot": {
    "description": "immersion foot title header"
  },
  "immersionFootDef": "Immersion foot is when the foot gets damaged by exposure to cold, wet conditions. It can happen when wearing wet shoes and socks without changing them",
  "@immersionFootDef": {
    "description": "def for immersion foot"
  },
  "immersionFootLabel": "The feet are damaged because of being wet and cold for a long time",
  "@immersionFootLabel": {
    "description": "immersion foot label header"
  },
  "immersionFootImages": "Click here for images of immersion foot",
  "@immersionFootImages": {
    "description": "images of immersion foot"
  },
  "immersionFootImage1": "Foot is very wrinkly, wet and pale",
  "@immersionFootImage1": {
    "description": "images of immersion foot"
  },
  "immersionFootImage2": "The skin is discolored, very wrinkly and wet; some redness is appearing under the toes",
  "@immersionFootImage2": {
    "description": "images of immersion foot"
  },
  "immersionFootImage3": "Foot is wrinkly, red, seems slightly swollen",
  "@immersionFootImage3": {
    "description": "images of immersion foot"
  },
  "immersionFootImage4": "Feet have swollen toes and blisters",
  "@immersionFootImage4": {
    "description": "images of immersion foot"
  },
  "immersionFootImage5": "The feet are very discolored, darker and swollen",
  "@immersionFootImage5": {
    "description": "images of immersion foot"
  },
  "immersionFootPreventionHeader": "Preventing immersion foot",
  "@immersionFootPreventionHeader": {
    "description": "prevention for immersion foot header"
  },
  "immersionFootPrevention": "● Always keep your feet clean and dry\n● Have extra pairs of socks and change your socks when they are wet 🧦💧\n● If your feet are wet and cold, try to find a warm place where you can take off your shoes to dry out your feet. While you do this, you can remove the soles of your shoes to help them dry out faster",
  "@immersionFootPrevention": {
    "description": "prevention for immersion foot"
  },
  "immersionFootSxHeader": "Immersion foot symptoms",
  "@immersionFootSxHeader": {
    "description": "immersionFoot sx header"
  },
  "immersionFootSx": "● At first, feet appear pale or grayish ⚪️, with wrinkly skin and cold to the touch ❄️\n● They will feel numb (loss of sensation)\n● As it gets worse, feet become red, swollen and very painful 🔴\n● Blisters can appear",
  "@immersionFootSx": {
    "description": "immersionFoot sx"
  },
  "immersionFootTxHeader": "Immersion foot treatment",
  "@immersionFootTxHeader": {
    "description": "tx for immersion foot header"
  },
  "immersionFootTx": "● Go to a warm and dry place, remove shoes and socks\n● Do not rub your feet, the skin is very delicate (you can lightly pat them dry with a clean towel)\n● Do not put hot water on your feet\n● Your feet need to warm up slowly and to air dry\n● As your feet rewarm, it might hurt — this is normal. Your feet might look red and swollen\n● Try to stay seated and to keep your feet raised to help reduce the swelling",
  "@immersionFootTx": {
    "description": "tx for immersion foot"
  },
  "immersionFootWarning": "As your feet warm up and dry, they should go back to their normal color and appearance. If you see no improvement after a few hours, seek medical attention",
  "@immersionFootWarning": {
    "description": "tx warning for immersion foot"
  },
  "ingrownNail": "Ingrown nail",
  "@ingrownNail": {
    "description": "ingrown nail title header"
  },
  "ingrownNailtDef": "An ingrown nail is when the corner of the toenail grows into the surrounding skin, which can cause pain and damage the skin. It often happens on the big toe",
  "@ingrownNailtDef": {
    "description": "def for ingrown nail"
  },
  "ingrownNailLabel": "The corner of the toenail is growing into the skin",
  "@ingrownNailLabel": {
    "description": "ingrown nail label header"
  },
  "ingrownNailImages": "Click here to see images of ingrown toenails",
  "@ingrownNailImages": {
    "description": "images of ingrown nails"
  },
  "ingrownNailImage1": "The edge of the nail is curving into the skin of the toe",
  "@ingrownNailImage1": {
    "description": "images of ingrown nails"
  },
  "ingrownNailImage2": "The nail is curved into the skin; the surrounding skin is very red and swollen",
  "@ingrownNailImage2": {
    "description": "images of ingrown nails"
  },
  "ingrownNailImage3": "Blood has dried where the nail has curved into the skin. There is redness and swelling spreading from the site; this toe might be infected",
  "@ingrownNailImage3": {
    "description": "images of ingrown nails"
  },
  "ingrownNailPreventionHeader": "Preventing ingrown nails",
  "@ingrownNailPreventionHeader": {
    "description": "prevention for ingrown nails header"
  },
  "ingrownNailPrevention": "● Always cut your toenails with a proper nail clipper\n● Cut your nails in a straight line — it's OK if the corners of the nails are a bit longer\n● Do not round the nails as this can encourage the nail to curve\n● You can use a nail file to smooth out any sharp edges or corners\n● Avoid shoes or socks that are too tight",
  "@ingrownNailPrevention": {
    "description": "prevention for ingrown nails"
  },
  "ingrownNailSxHeader": "Ingrown nail symptoms",
  "@ingrownNailSxHeader": {
    "description": "ingrown nail sx header"
  },
  "ingrownNailSx": "● Nails curving inwards ➰\n● Pain\n● Redness 🔴\n● Swelling\n● Ingrown toenails are at a high risk of becoming infected",
  "@ingrownNailSx": {
    "description": "ingrown nail sx"
  },
  "ingrownNailTxHeader": "Ingrown nail treatment",
  "@ingrownNailTxHeader": {
    "description": "tx for ingrown nail header"
  },
  "ingrownNailTx": "● Seek a medical professional as they can help lift the nail and remove the part that is growing into the toe\n● Clean the affected foot with warm water and mild soap every day",
  "@ingrownNailTx": {
    "description": "tx for ingrown nail"
  },
  "ingrownNailWarning": "If you have diabetes, poor circulation, a weakened immune system or other health conditions, you may be at higher risk for skin infections",
  "@ingrownNailWarning": {
    "description": "tx warning for ingrown nail"
  },
