  },
  "nailFungusTxHeader": "Treatment for nail fungus",
  "@nailFungusTxHeader": {
    "description": "nail fungus tx header"
  },
  "nailFungusTx": "There are antifungal creams that exist for mild cases of nail fungus. Always ask the pharmacist for help\n\nFor more severe cases, seek a doctor",
  "@nailFungusTx": {
    "description": "nail fungus tx "
  },
  "nailFungusPreventionHeader": "Preventing nail fungus",
  "@nailFungusPreventionHeader": {
    "description": "prevention step for nail fungus header"
  },
  "nailFungusPrevention": "● Keep feet dry and clean\n● Change socks often 🧦\n● You can use desiccating foot powders to help keep feet dry\n● When using shared showers, try to wear sandals or flip-flops 🩴\n● Do not share nail clippers",
  "@nailFungusPrevention": {
    "description": "prevention step for nail fungus"
  },
  "nailFungusPreventionWarning": "● Try to keep feet clean and dry\n● Seek medical help, especially if you notice bleeding around the nail 🩸 or if walking becomes painful",
  "@nailFungusPreventionWarning": {
    "description": "steps if they catch nail fungus"
  },
  "normalDischarge": "Click here to see images of wound discharge",
  "@normalDischarge": {
    "description": "dialog box for normal vs abnormal discharge"
  },
  "normalWound": "Normal wounds may have some redness and pain\nThey might also have some discharge that is clear, light yellow or light pink",
  "@normalWound": {
    "description": "normal wound info"
  },
  "skinGeneralHeader": "How to protect your skin",
  "@skinGeneralHeader": {
    "description": "general skin maintenance header"
  },
  "skinGeneral": "● Keep skin washed and dry \n● Always protect any wounds with bandages 🩹 and look at them every day for signs of infection\n● Use moisturizers or just simply Vaseline to keep skin moist 🧴\n● Stay hydrated by drinking water 💧\n● Try to eat well, this helps you keep healthy skin",
  "@skinGeneral": {
    "description": "general skin maintenance"
  },
  "skinGeneralSummerHeader": "How to protect your skin during the summer",
  "@skinGeneralSummerHeader": {
    "description": "general skin maintenance — summer header"
  },
  "skinGeneralSummer": "● Use hats 🧢, loose and light-colored clothing, and stay in the shade\n● Wear sunscreen every day if you can, even if you have dark skin\n● Use sunscreen with an SPF of 30 or more. You need an amount of cream about the size of a 2$ coin to cover your face\n● Reapply sunscreen at least every 2 hours 🧴☀️\n● Stay hydrated by drinking water 💧",
  "@skinGeneralSummer": {
    "description": "general skin maintenance — summer"
  },
  "skinGeneralWinterHeader": "How to protect your skin during the winter",
  "@skinGeneralWinterHeader": {
    "description": "general skin maintenance — winter header"
  },
  "skinGeneralWinter": "● Wear multiple layers of clothing and always keep your fingers ✋, ears 👂, and nose 👃 covered\n● Avoid any wet clothing\n● Moisturizers or Vaseline can help keep your skin protected and avoid dryness\n● It is possible to get a sunburn during the winter, so wear sunscreen on your face if it is sunny\n● When it is very cold (–15 °C or less), find shelter\n● Eat well, avoid alcohol 🍺🍷❌",
  "@skinGeneralWinter": {
    "description": "general skin maintenance — winter"
  },
  "feetGeneralHeader": "How to protect your feet",
  "@feetGeneralHeader": {
    "description": "general feet maintenance header"
  },
  "feetGeneral": "● Wash your feet daily with warm water and mild soap\n● Keep your feet nice and dry, especially between your toes\n● Apply moisturizing lotion to your feet\n● Wear shoes and socks that fit you well — not too big, not too tight\n● Inspect your feet every day for any wounds",
  "@feetGeneral": {
    "description": "general feet maintenance"
  },
  "nailGeneralHeader": "How to keep your toenails healthy",
  "@nailGeneralHeader": {
    "description": "general nails maintenance header"
  },
  "nailGeneral": "● Toe nails should never be too long — they should not go beyond the point of your toes\n● Use proper nail cutters to cut nails\n● Never share nail cutting tools\n● Cut nails in a straight line, do not round them\n● Use a nail file to smooth any sharp edges",
  "@nailGeneral": {
    "description": "general nails maintenance"
  },
  "sunburn": "Sunburns",
  "@sunburn": {
    "description": "title header for sunburns"
  },
  "sunburnLabel": "Skin damage from the sun",
  "@sunburnLabel": {
    "description": "label header for sunburns"
  },
  "sunburnDef": "Sunburns happen when you spend too long in the sun without any protection. The ultraviolet rays cause damage to the skin",
  "@sunburnDef": {
    "description": "definition sunburns"
  },
  "sunburnSxHeader": "Sunburn symptoms",
  "@sunburnSxHeader": {
    "description": "sunburn sx header"
  },
  "sunburnSx": "● Redness 🔴\n● Skin is hot to the touch 🔥\n● Pain\n● Symptoms usually develop several hours after being in the sun and can last a few days\n● After a few days, skin will begin to peel, this is normal",
  "@sunburnSx": {
    "description": "sunburn sx"
  },
  "severeSunburnSx": "In cases of severe sunburn, there may be blistering, severe pain or fever. Seek medical attention",
  "@severeSunburnSx": {
    "description": "severe sunburn sx"
  },
  "sunburnImages": "Click here to see images of sunburns",
  "@sunburnImages": {
    "description": "dialog box for sunburn images "
  },
  "sunburnImage1": "Skin is very red",
  "@sunburnImage1": {
    "description": "images of sunburns "
  },
  "sunburnImage2": "Skin is red with small fluid-filled blisters",
  "@sunburnImage2": {
    "description": "images of sunburns "
  },
  "sunburnImage3": "Very severe sunburn with significant blisters and redness - this requires medical care",
  "@sunburnImage3": {
    "description": "images of sunburns "
  },
  "sunburnImage4": "Sunburn that is a few days old, skin has begun peeling",
  "@sunburnImage4": {
    "description": "images of sunburns "
  },
  "sunburnImage5": "Healed sunburn with peeling skin",
  "@sunburnImage5": {
    "description": "images of sunburns "
  },
  "sunburnTxHeader": "Treatment for sunburns",
  "@sunburnTxHeader": {
    "description": "sunburn tx header"
  },
  "sunburnTx": "● Stay out of the sun\n● Apply cool compresses to affected skin or take a cold shower 🚿\n● Never apply ice directly to the skin 🧊❌\n● Ask the pharmacist to find products that can help soothe sunburns\n● Never scratch or pick the affected skin",
  "@sunburnTx": {
    "description": "sunburn tx "
  },
  "sunburnPreventionHeader": "Preventing sunburns",
  "@sunburnPreventionHeader": {
    "description": "header for sunburn prevention"
  },
  "sunburnPrevention": "● Avoid the sun and stay in the shade, especially when the sun's light is the strongest (between 10 AM to 4 PM)\n● Wear a wide-brimmed hat and light-colored long sleeves to cover your skin 🧢👕👖\n● Apply sunscreen with an SPF of 30 or more to exposed skin. Use an amount of cream about the size of a 2$ coin to cover your face\n● Reapply sunscreen at least every 2 hours 🧴☀️",
  "@sunburnPrevention": {
    "description": "prevention step for sunburns"
  },
  "sxOfInfectionHeader": "Signs of infection",
  "@sxOfInfectionHeader": {
    "description": "header for sx of infections"
  },
  "sxOfInfection": "● Skin is red or darker than normal 🔴\n● Swelling\n● Warm feeling 🔥\n● Pain\n● Bad smell\n● Visible pus (thick yellow, greenish or gray fluid)\n● Fever 🤒",
  "@sxOfInfection": {
    "description": "sx of infections"
  },
  "whatInfection": "An infection happens when bacteria (germs) get into a wound. This can be dangerous to your health",
  "@whatInfection": {
    "description": "infection definition"
  }
}